I remember Chacha's words.
"Turn right at the next corner."
"And then go straight."
I go towards the corner.
I turn right from there.
Now I walk absolutely straight.
There are many tall buildings here.
This street is very crowded.
I walk towards the sea.
Suddenly I feel a cool breeze.
The row of buildings ends.
There is a very wide road in front of me.
I cross that road.
I step onto a wide path by the sea.
This is Marine Drive.
This place is very open.
The vast sea is in front of me.
The breeze is very fresh.
I take a deep breath.
I am very happy.
